  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q6",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "$(18,30,n)$ is a Pythagorean triad. Find the value(s) of $n$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$n=24$ only. Taking $n$ as the largest number gives $\\sqrt{1224}$, which is not a whole number.",
      "worked": "If $30$ is the largest number:\n$$\\begin{align*}18^2+n^2&=30^2\\\\n^2&=30^2-18^2\\\\n^2&=900-324\\\\n&=\\sqrt{576}=24\\end{align*}$$\nIf $n$ is the largest number:\n$$\\begin{align*}18^2+30^2&=n^2\\\\n^2&=324+900\\\\n&=\\sqrt{1224}\\end{align*}$$\nSince $34^2<1224<35^2$, $\\sqrt{1224}$ is not a whole number. Therefore, $n=24$ is the only answer.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 52
  },
